WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:06.860
Yokohama

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.810
Shopping Trip Log

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:13.780
Gone shopping
in Yokohama

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.200
Some years ago,

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.970
the owner…

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.380
entrusted me with the shop

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.540
and went away somewhere.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.530
Where to? What for?

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.580
Will he return someday?

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.900
I think it’s good that I’m a robot.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.840
No matter how long it takes, I can wait.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:27.100
Gone shopping
in Yokohama

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:27.100
To Alpha
I’m glad to see you are doing well.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.420
I was just out for a bit to buy a new rake.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.330
The weather didn’t agree with me.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.140
Ah, I won’t make it home in time.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:12.900
Rain and the Aftermath

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.570
That was close.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.310
I’m sorry for troubling you.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:31.020
Don’t you worry about a thing.
I know a good hospital.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.480
The doc’s a friend of mine.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.860
She’s much better than someone in a big hospital far away.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.680
Doctor…?

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.520
She’ll be just fine.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.400
The lightning only struck on the outside.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.900
It’ll be two or three days before she can leave the hospital though,

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.070
since her skin and hair need to be replaced.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.910
It’s been a while since I’ve taken care of a robot patient.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.080
Two or three days?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.000
But she seemed to be badly hurt.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.920
You can go talk to her if you want.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.550
Hi, Ojisan.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:33.180
The doc told me you’d be well enough to leave in three days, but…

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.690
It looks serious, but she just changed the primary skin coating.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.390
Um, Ojisan?

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.900
Can you keep this a secret from Takahiro?

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.950
Sure. But he’ll find out when we come to pick you up.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.450
I’ll be back tomorrow to see how you’re doin’.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.330
Oh, do ya need somethin’?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.040
I would appreciate it if you could bring me a change of clothes.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.880
The back door should be unlocked.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.760
Alrighty, I’ll bring some.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.050
Now, ya try and get some rest.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:14.970
Thank you.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.820
The primary coating was finished the next day.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.340
My my.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:54.010
Worried about the rough edges?

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.310
Don’t worry about it.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.440
It’ll feel a bit fluffy since we’ve only finished the primary coating.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.990
Your skin will be soft and smooth after the secondary coating and the finishing touches.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.950
Oh, I see.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:14.160
I replaced the hair too, since most of it was damaged.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.030
Wha?

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.490
It’s the same type of hair you had before.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.830
You wouldn’t like it if the color were changed, right?

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.000
I feel relieved.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.750
I don’t know how I can thank you.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.550
Save your thanks for that ojisan who brought you in.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:39.220
I should be able to finish you up tomorrow, so you’ll be able to leave by the next day.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.820
Tears are beginning to form in my eyes.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:01.750
My lachrymal glands were designed solely for keeping my optical tissues moist, but…

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:09.920
I’ve had this happen to me before, when I was playing the lute alone.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.430
But this feels different somehow.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.310
I like this feeling as well.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.060
On the day of my return…

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.230
Alpha, are you ready to go back?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.780
Uh… did you, um, change your hairstyle?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.410
It’s… it’s not what you think!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.420
Ah! What happened to your hair?

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.510
It’ll be like that until it settles down.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:54.170
H-how long will that take?

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.430
Well, it shouldn’t take longer than a week.

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.220
One…

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:01.140
One week?!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.640
Tears begin to form in my eyes again,

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.270
but it’s a whole different feeling this time.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.030
Ojisan, um… thank you very much for everything.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:18.530
What’re you talkin’ about? Save your thanks for the doc.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.540
Well, I don’t know how I can ever pay you back,

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.080
so please come by the café, and I’ll serve you two some free coffee.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.710
Oh, don’t be so uptight about it, will ya?

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.040
You’re like family to us anyway.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.420
What’s wrong? What’s wrong?
What’re ya cryin’ for?

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:39.800
Oh, no, it’s just that I’m so grateful.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:57.480
Oops, I haven’t prepared the coffee yet!

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.090
The beans are overcooked.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.820
I burned the beans a bit…

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.200
But I can still smell the same familiar aroma of coffee.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.600
Mmm. Smells delicious.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.280
One.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:32.820
Two.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:43.960
Five.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:55.930
Smells great.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.230
I can hear the sea.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:06.330
Wherever the swaying of waves may take me…

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:15.970
Endlessly looking up into the sky

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:24.350
Wandering around, dreaming of being a fish

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:33.440
There, a single trail of wind was blowing

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:33.610
The Wind Was Blowing

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:49.250
Following the running cloud

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:59.220
Escaping the old street

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:07.140
Wandering around with no place to go

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:16.190
There, a single trail of wind was blowing

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:45.310
Wandering around with no place to go

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:54.360
There, a single trail of wind was blowing

00:18:54.770 --> 00:19:03.490
There, a single trail of wind was blowing

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:09.540
The wind was blowing…

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.180
As I stroked the smooth surface of the camera…

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:56.210
…morning had given way to afternoon
before I knew it.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.300
I remember now!

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:46.260
I can’t believe I had forgotten
about it all this time:

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.520
The place my owner took me to
when I first arrived here.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:57.940
Ojisan—!

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:01.030
Hiya.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.320
Where are ya off to?

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.320
A private event!

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.330
What d’ya mean?

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.340
If I remember correctly…

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:24.840
I last went there when
I visited the northern town.

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:34.640
All I have now are fragmented images and sweet memories, but…

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.110
I hope I can get there before the sun sets.

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:19.690
I knew it! This is it!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:26.570
It feels a bit different, but…

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:29.160
this is the place.

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:35.120
Alpha-san?

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:40.670
I thought it was you.

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:41.630
Doctor?

00:22:42.310 --> 00:22:44.170
Do you come here often?

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:47.720
Well, not really.
I think I came here once before.

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:49.970
Doctor, what are you doing here today?

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:52.430
I just stopped by on my way to the northern town.

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:57.390
Do you come here often?

00:22:57.390 --> 00:22:58.350
Sometimes.

00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:11.200
As the sun sets to the west,

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:16.080
I can’t stop the excitement rising in me.

00:25:14.120 --> 00:25:17.490
It’s… It’s so beautiful.

00:25:17.870 --> 00:25:19.030
Yes, it is.

00:25:19.280 --> 00:25:22.910
Many of the old street lights are still left here.

00:25:26.040 --> 00:25:31.300
When you last came here, you probably missed watching the night scenery.

00:25:42.010 --> 00:25:44.810
The street lights come to life…

00:25:47.310 --> 00:25:51.440
where there are only trees… and the ocean.

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:56.280
The lights that once shone so brightly with purpose…

00:25:58.660 --> 00:25:59.780
now shine…

00:26:01.530 --> 00:26:03.370
for the sole purpose of shining.

00:26:08.710 --> 00:26:10.920
Though not many get to see this,

00:26:10.920 --> 00:26:13.050
isn’t it good to have such unique flowers around?

00:26:57.800 --> 00:26:59.930
These flowers of light…

00:27:01.690 --> 00:27:03.100
left behind by the former residents.

00:27:04.310 --> 00:27:11.270
Yokosuka Cruise

00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:37.840
The festival-like world…

00:27:38.510 --> 00:27:41.970
has slowly settled to a leisurely pace.

00:27:46.600 --> 00:27:48.100
To think that an era…

00:27:48.930 --> 00:27:51.810
would reach its twilight so pleasantly.

00:27:56.270 --> 00:28:01.110
The dangerous times have since been called the “Age of Evening Calm.”

00:28:16.630 --> 00:28:24.890
I will probably keep watching this twilight world… as long as time flows.
